=== ending_hero ===
You step into the sunlight with a cardboard trophy and a lantern that has opinions.
The mailbox {Facts ? kicked_mailbox: pretends not to see you|cheers, in mail}.
Score: {score} of {MAX_SCORE}, in {TURNS()} turns.
You have {&won|won, technically|completed the demo}. The dragon files this under "fine".
-> END

=== ending_petty ===
You won. The mailbox has already written a one-star review.
The trophy is slightly dented where a tiny brass door kicked it back.
Score: {score}. The narrator awards you an extra zero for manners.
-> END

=== ending_grue ===
{GRUE_WARNING}
A grue clears its throat apologetically, then eats you. It is nothing personal. It is in the job description.
Score: {score}. Lantern status: {lamp_looks()}.
-> END

=== ending_eaten ===
You are eaten, or at least thoroughly defeated, by something with more union protection than you.
It thanks you for your time. It means it.
Score: {score}.
-> END

=== ending_lost ===
You sit down in the maze and wait to be rescued.
Nobody comes. Eventually the passages adopt you.
Score: {score}. You are, in a sense, home.
-> END

=== ending_quit ===
You QUIT, like a coward, or like a person with things to do.
The lantern stays {lamp_looks()}. The sandwich, if any, is not refunded.
Score: {score}. Thanks for playing.
-> END
